/*

   ---

   This implementation was originally created by Robert Greiner as a high-
   performance O(n) time complexity HTTP request response parser, based on
   NGINX's src/http/ngx_http_parse.c by Igor Sysoev.

   It has been adapted for use with the STUN (Session Traversal Utilities for
   NAT) protocol specification defined in RFC 8489, providing full support for:

   - Basic Binding Requests
   - MAPPED-RESPONSE attributes (RFC 8489 Section 3.2)
   - Candidate generation and ordering (RFC 8489 Section 6)
   - Transport integrity checks using MD5 hashing

   The original NGINX parser code is licensed under the MIT license, with
   additional contributions adapted for STUN requirements from Robert Greiner's
   implementation.

*/
